      'The bake runs on the GPU. One compute workgroup per probe casts rays (a spherical Fibonacci set, randomly rotated each sweep) against an analytic copy of the room: the same few dozen boxes and the sphere the rasteriser draws. Each hit is shaded with the sun (an exact shadow ray), the lamp, or the sky if the ray leaves through the window. From the second bounce on, the hit also gets the previous bounce\'s probe light. Rays are projected onto SH and summed in workgroup memory. Every sweep over the grid is averaged into the volume, so the result converges over 48 sweeps, after which the bake stops. When the light changes, the volume keeps a few sweeps of history and re-converges a few probes per frame. Engines bake offline with path tracing, but the structure is the same.',
